# STREAMING_CHUNK:Disabling directory browsing and restricting direct access to sensitive files...

# Prevent directory listings
Options -Indexes

# Protect sensitive environment and system files from HTTP access
<FilesMatch "^\.env|bootstrap\.php|PROMPT_SPECIFICATION\.md|composer\.(json|lock)|phinx\.php">
    <IfModule mod_authz_core.c>
        Require all denied
    </IfModule>
    <IfModule !mod_authz_core.c>
        Order allow,deny
        Deny from all
    </IfModule>
</FilesMatch>

# STREAMING_CHUNK:Configuring URL rewriting engine and public directory routing...

# URL Rewriting to public/index.php
<IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
    RewriteEngine On
    RewriteBase /

    # If the request is already pointing to public/, pass through
    RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} ^/public/ [NC]
    RewriteRule ^ - [L]

    # Serve static assets directly if they exist in the public directory
    RewriteCond %{DOCUMENT_ROOT}/public%{REQUEST_URI} -f [OR]
    RewriteCond %{DOCUMENT_ROOT}/public%{REQUEST_URI} -d
    RewriteRule ^(.*)$ public/$1 [L]

    # Route all other non-existing files and requests through public/index.php
    RewriteRule ^ public/index.php [QSA,L]
</IfModule>
```eof

The `.htaccess` file is now ready in the root directory. It ensures that Apache safely redirects all Web traffic directly to `public/index.php` while blocking external access to sensitive configuration files like `.env` and `bootstrap.php`.